Employees enroll in a session with a fixed positive seat capacity. Emails are trimmed and lowercased, then checked for a basic email shape. Duplicate enrollment is rejected. Cancellation removes an existing enrollment. Attendance contains confirmed employees in enrollment order.

Domain failures throw `DeskError` with stable `code` values: INVALID_SESSION, DUPLICATE_SESSION, NOT_FOUND, INVALID_EMAIL, ALREADY_ENROLLED, FULL, NOT_ENROLLED, NOT_OFFERED. Portal submission translates domain errors into failure replies; malformed JSON shapes produce BAD_REQUEST. Unexpected programming errors propagate. For desk operations, session existence is checked before email validation. Failed operations do not change state. Each desk owns its data; seeds, returned enrollments, rosters and attendance arrays may be mutated by callers without altering stored data.

Sessions start with admissions open, exposed as `admissionsOpen` on roster snapshots. `setAdmissions(sessionId, open)` pauses or resumes admissions. While paused, enrollment throws ADMISSIONS_CLOSED before email or duplicate checks; cancellation remains available without offering seats to waiting employees. Reopening offers all available seats to the waiting list in join order. Repeating an admissions state is harmless.

Enrollment accepts optional `{ waitlist: boolean }`: free seats confirm immediately, while a full session requires opt-in to join the waiting list. Confirmed or offered cancellations offer released seats to the earliest waiting employees only while admissions are open. Offers reserve capacity until accepted, declined or cancelled; they do not expire. `acceptOffer` confirms an offered entry even while admissions are paused, and `declineOffer` removes it, offering the released seat to the next waiting employee only while open. Both operations require an offered entry and check session existence before normalizing email. Directory identity is unique across all three statuses; rosters include all, and attendance includes confirmed employees only. Portal submissions accept an optional boolean `waitlist` field and reject other present values with BAD_REQUEST.

The desk and portal exports are used only by this application and its tests; there are no external package consumers. Tests execute built JavaScript from dist. Keep the attendance export and portal submission consistent with the application rules.

